/**

@page applications_exahype2_thunderstorm Thunderstorm

This example implements the gravity-wave scenario of Snively and Pasko (2003),
“Breaking of thunderstorm-generated gravity waves as a source of short-period ducted
waves at mesopause altitudes” (doi:10.1029/2003GL018436).
A background atmosphere is prescribed from CSV profiles (density, temperature, composition),
and forced by an idealised thunderstorm source region.

The setup couples two solvers:

1. a compressible Euler solver for the background atmosphere, including hydrostatic balance,
open side boundaries, and reflective / radiative vertical boundaries, and

2. a diffusion solver that evolves velocity and temperature with height-dependent viscosity
and thermal diffusivity

Density profile:
@image html applications/gravity-waves/thunderstorm/rho.jpg

*/
